config VIDEO_MTK_ISP
	tristate "MediaTek MT6735 camera ISP character driver"
	depends on MEDIA_SUPPORT
	depends on VIDEO_DEV
	depends on COMMON_CLK
	depends on OF
	depends on PM
	help
	  Character driver for the MediaTek MT6735 / MT6737T camera ISP
	  ("camera-isp").  It implements the downstream libcamdrv ABI
	  published in include/uapi/linux/mtk_isp.h: register window mmap,
	  register read/write, the hold-register write buffers, per-user
	  interrupt status/wait/mark/clear with user keys, the Pass-1 /
	  Pass-1-D / CAMSV DMA buffer rings with SOF-time base address and
	  RCNT_INC programming, the Pass-2 early-done queue, reset, register
	  scenario and burst queue controls.

	  Frame completion is derived exclusively from the ISP interrupt
	  lines; no timer or polled completion path exists.  Interrupt
	  status registers are read-to-clear, so they are sampled once per
	  interrupt and never from a diagnostic path.

	  The ISP power domain and the IMGSYS clock gates are shared with
	  the mtk-imgsys platform driver; this driver takes its own
	  references so register access is always safe.

	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the module will
	  be called mtk-isp.
